.policy "django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table" revision 1
.description "Avoid column type changes that make PostgreSQL rewrite an existing large table, such as integer to bigint or a shorter length limit; the rewrite blocks reads and writes."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. `ALTER TABLE … ALTER COLUMN … TYPE` takes an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock and rewrites the
// table and its indexes unless the old type is binary coercible to the new one (PostgreSQL, ALTER TABLE notes;
// Squawk "changing-column-type"). A migration's AlterField says only the new field; the old one comes from the app's
// migration history (the library's dj_field_old): the nearest earlier definition of the same model and field (a
// CreateModel `fields` item, an AddField or an AlterField, followed back through a RenameField onto the name) in a
// migration applied before this one (dj_mig_ran_before, which also reads a dependency on a migration a squash
// replaces as the squash) or earlier in this one, with no other definition of the field between them.
// Column types are resolved, not matched by name: a field class is Django's own (django.db.models,
// django.contrib.postgres.fields, ...) or a class of the run derived from one with no `db_type` override on the way
// (dj_custom_field: `class MoneyField(models.DecimalField)` is numeric); a ForeignKey or OneToOneField column has the
// type of its target's primary key at that point of the history (dj_field_at of the relation call), or, when that
// history is not in the run's app, the one type every definition of the target's key has.
// Reported:
//   - integers of another width: AutoField/IntegerField/PositiveIntegerField (integer), SmallAutoField/
//     SmallIntegerField/PositiveSmallIntegerField (smallint), BigAutoField/BigIntegerField/PositiveBigIntegerField
//     (bigint), either way; the DEFAULT_AUTO_FIELD switch to BigAutoField is one (pretix's `0246_bigint.py`). Django
//     changes the ForeignKey columns that point at a widened primary key in the same statement, so the pk's
//     AlterField stands for them; an IntegerField made a ForeignKey to a bigint key, or a ForeignKey retargeted to a
//     key of another type, is one too;
//   - a varchar (CharField, SlugField, EmailField, URLField, FileField, ImageField, FilePathField, by their
//     max_length or Django's default for it) that gets shorter, or a text or unlimited varchar that gets a limit
//     (TextField → CharField(max_length=n));
//   - a DecimalField whose decimal_places change or whose max_digits shrink;
//   - any other change of PostgreSQL type: CharField → IntegerField, IntegerField → CharField, FloatField →
//     DecimalField, DateField → DateTimeField, TextField → JSONField, ...
//     AlterField("order", "id", models.BigAutoField(...))  after  ("id", models.AutoField(...))             reported
//     AlterField("order", "number", models.CharField(max_length=10))  after  CharField(max_length=20)        reported
//     AlterField("order", "customer_ref", models.ForeignKey(to="shop.customer"))  after  IntegerField(), with
//       customer.id a BigAutoField                                                                          reported
// Left alone, as PostgreSQL changes them in the catalog only, or as they are not type changes: a longer or unlimited
// varchar, varchar → text, CharField ↔ SlugField/EmailField/URLField without a shorter limit, a DecimalField with
// more max_digits and the same decimal_places, the same type with other null/blank/default/choices/db_index/unique
// (other hazards); a ForeignKey whose target key keeps its type.
//     AlterField("order", "note", models.CharField(max_length=200))  after  CharField(max_length=100)        not reported
//     AlterField("order", "ref", models.TextField())  after  CharField(max_length=40)                        not reported
// Also left alone: a model the same migration creates (dj_mig_creates), a field with no earlier definition in the
// run (a squashed history, another app's migrations), a SeparateDatabaseAndState's state_operations (which still
// count as definitions for later AlterFields), migrations in test directories, a field class from a third party
// (`django_countries.fields.CountryField`) or one that overrides db_type; the length or precision of a project field
// class with an `__init__` on the way (dj_custom_field_init: InvenTree's InvenTreeURLField forces max_length=2000), whose
// arguments may not be its column's; a max_length or max_digits that is no integer literal, a relation whose
// target key is unknown or has had several types; a model the project's code reads as one row (dj_one_row:
// `M.objects.get()`, a lazy-singleton `M.objects.first()` beside a `create()`, `M.get_solo()`), whose rewrite is
// instant; a run that configures MySQL and names no PostgreSQL database (dj_mysql_only), where other changes copy the
// table and this classification does not hold.
//     ApplicationConfiguration.objects.all().first()  in config.py; AlterField("applicationconfiguration", ...)  not reported
// Gaps: a RunSQL `ALTER COLUMN … TYPE` is not a definition; a renamed model loses its history (silent); relation
// targets are matched by model name across the run; a table the previous migration created is reported though it may
// still be empty; the rule cannot see a table's size, so a small table's rewrite is reported too (hence log mode, off
// by default); a team that migrates with the application stopped pays only upgrade time; ArrayField, citext and
// hstore changes are not judged.

#include "lib/django.rerail"

.violation TypeChangeRewrites(at: node, m: symbol, x: symbol, old: symbol, new: symbol) "{m}.{x} goes from {old} to {new}: PostgreSQL rewrites the table under a lock that blocks reads and writes. On a large table add a column, backfill, swap; keep it for a small table."

TypeChangeRewrites(f, m, x, lo, ln) :- dj_field_old(o, fo), ar_alter(o, _, _, m, x, f), ar_rewrite(fo, f),
    ar_label(fo, lo), ar_label(f, ln).

// ---- the change --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ar_alter(o, d, i, m, x, f): AlterField o, item i of migration d (not test code, not a squashed migration), changes
// field x of model m (not created in d, not a one-row table) to field call f, in a run that may use PostgreSQL. A
// squashed migration (`replaces = [...]`) copies operations that already ran on every database that applied the
// migrations it replaces; it runs them only on a database that applied none of them, usually a new one, and its
// author did not choose them.
.decl ar_alter(o: node, d: number, i: number, m: symbol, x: symbol, f: node)
ar_alter(o, d, i, m, x, f) :- dj_alterfield(o, d, i, m, x), !dj_mig_attr(d, "replaces", _), !dj_mig_creates(d, m),
    !dj_one_row(m), !dj_mysql_only(), dj_mig_arg(o, "field", f).

// ---- types -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ar_call(f): the field calls judged: an AlterField's, its nearest earlier definition's, and the target key
// definitions of the relations among them.
.decl ar_call(f: node)
ar_call(f) :- ar_alter(o, _, _, _, _, f), dj_field_old(o, _).
ar_call(f) :- ar_alter(o, _, _, _, _, _), dj_field_old(o, f).
ar_call(k) :- ar_call(f), ar_cls(f, t), dj_fk_class(t), ar_fk_key(f, k).
// ar_cls(f, t): call f constructs Django's field class t, or a class of the run derived from it (dj_custom_field);
// ar_own(f): Django's own class, whose defaults (a CharField's missing max_length) the rule knows.
.decl ar_cls(f: node, t: symbol)
ar_cls(f, t) :- ar_call(f), ar_own(f, t).
ar_cls(f, t) :- ar_call(f), ar_custom(f, q), dj_custom_field(q, t).
.decl ar_own(f: node, t: symbol)
ar_own(f, t) :- ar_call(f), kind(f, "call"), field(f, "function", e), sym_of(e, q), split_dot(q, mo, t),
    dj_field_module(mo).
.decl ar_custom(f: node, q: symbol)
ar_custom(f, q) :- ar_call(f), kind(f, "call"), field(f, "function", e), sym_of(e, q), dj_custom_field(q, _).
// ar_args(f): call f's arguments are its column's parameters: Django's own class, or a project class with no
// `__init__` on the way (dj_custom_field_init), which could rewrite them.
.decl ar_args(f: node)
ar_args(f) :- ar_own(f, _).
ar_args(f) :- ar_custom(f, q), !dj_custom_field_init(q).
// ar_fk_key(f, k): relation call f's column is its target's primary key, defined by field call k. For an
// AlterField's new relation, the key's definition at that point of the history (dj_field_at); otherwise (an old
// definition, whose column followed every later change of the key, or a target outside the app's history) any
// definition of the key, which must all have one type (ar_fk_type).
.decl ar_fk_key(f: node, k: node)
ar_fk_key(f, k) :- ar_alter(_, _, _, _, _, f), dj_field_at(f, k).
ar_fk_key(f, k) :- dj_fk_target(f, m), !ar_fk_at(f), dj_pk_call(m, k).
.decl ar_fk_at(f: node)
ar_fk_at(f) :- ar_alter(_, _, _, _, _, f), dj_field_at(f, _).
// ar_fk_type(f, y): relation call f's column has type y: the one type of its target keys, an integer or a uuid
// (a varchar or numeric key's parameters are not followed).
.decl ar_fk_type(f: node, y: symbol)
ar_fk_type(f, y) :- ar_fk_key(f, k), ar_base(k, y), y != "varchar", y != "numeric", !ar_fk_mixed(f), !ar_fk_opaque(f).
.decl ar_fk_mixed(f: node)
ar_fk_mixed(f) :- ar_fk_key(f, a), ar_fk_key(f, b), ar_base(a, x), ar_base(b, y), x != y.
.decl ar_fk_opaque(f: node)
ar_fk_opaque(f) :- ar_fk_key(f, k), !ar_base(k, _).
// ar_pg(t, y): Django field class t is PostgreSQL column type y.
.decl ar_pg(t: symbol, y: symbol)
ar_pg("AutoField", "integer"). ar_pg("IntegerField", "integer"). ar_pg("PositiveIntegerField", "integer").
ar_pg("SmallAutoField", "smallint"). ar_pg("SmallIntegerField", "smallint").
ar_pg("PositiveSmallIntegerField", "smallint").
ar_pg("BigAutoField", "bigint"). ar_pg("BigIntegerField", "bigint"). ar_pg("PositiveBigIntegerField", "bigint").
ar_pg("CharField", "varchar"). ar_pg("SlugField", "varchar"). ar_pg("EmailField", "varchar").
ar_pg("URLField", "varchar"). ar_pg("FileField", "varchar"). ar_pg("ImageField", "varchar").
ar_pg("FilePathField", "varchar"). ar_pg("TextField", "text").
ar_pg("DecimalField", "numeric"). ar_pg("FloatField", "double precision").
ar_pg("BooleanField", "boolean"). ar_pg("NullBooleanField", "boolean").
ar_pg("DateField", "date"). ar_pg("DateTimeField", "timestamp with time zone"). ar_pg("TimeField", "time").
ar_pg("DurationField", "interval"). ar_pg("UUIDField", "uuid"). ar_pg("JSONField", "jsonb").
ar_pg("BinaryField", "bytea"). ar_pg("GenericIPAddressField", "inet"). ar_pg("IPAddressField", "inet").
// ar_base(f, y): field call f makes a column of type y by its own class; ar_type(f, y): also a relation, by its key.
.decl ar_base(f: node, y: symbol)
ar_base(f, y) :- ar_cls(f, t), ar_pg(t, y).
.decl ar_type(f: node, y: symbol)
ar_type(f, y) :- ar_base(f, y).
ar_type(f, y) :- ar_cls(f, t), dj_fk_class(t), ar_fk_type(f, y).
// ar_deflen(t, n, s): varchar field class t without max_length is n (text s) characters long.
.decl ar_deflen(t: symbol, n: number, s: symbol)
ar_deflen("SlugField", 50, "50"). ar_deflen("EmailField", 254, "254"). ar_deflen("URLField", 200, "200").
ar_deflen("FileField", 100, "100"). ar_deflen("ImageField", 100, "100"). ar_deflen("FilePathField", 100, "100").
// ar_len(f, n, s): varchar call f has a limit of n characters (text s); ar_unlimited(f): it has none (a CharField
// without max_length, or max_length=None); ar_len_unknown(f): its max_length is no literal.
.decl ar_len(f: node, n: number, s: symbol)
ar_len(f, n, s) :- ar_type(f, "varchar"), ar_args(f), call_arg(f, -1, "max_length", v), kind(v, "integer"),
    text(v, s), n = to_number(s).
ar_len(f, n, s) :- ar_own(f, t), ar_deflen(t, n, s), !call_arg(f, -1, "max_length", _).
.decl ar_unlimited(f: node)
ar_unlimited(f) :- ar_own(f, "CharField"), !call_arg(f, -1, "max_length", _).
ar_unlimited(f) :- ar_type(f, "varchar"), ar_args(f), call_arg(f, -1, "max_length", v), kind(v, "none").
.decl ar_len_unknown(f: node)
ar_len_unknown(f) :- ar_type(f, "varchar"), !ar_len(f, _, _), !ar_unlimited(f).
// ar_dec(f, p, s, tp, ts): DecimalField call f has max_digits p and decimal_places s (texts tp, ts).
.decl ar_dec(f: node, p: number, s: number, tp: symbol, ts: symbol)
ar_dec(f, p, s, tp, ts) :- ar_type(f, "numeric"), ar_args(f), call_arg(f, -1, "max_digits", a), kind(a, "integer"),
    text(a, tp), call_arg(f, -1, "decimal_places", b), kind(b, "integer"), text(b, ts), p = to_number(tp),
    s = to_number(ts).
// ar_known(f): the rule knows call f's column type with all its parameters.
.decl ar_known(f: node)
ar_known(f) :- ar_type(f, y), y != "varchar", y != "numeric".
ar_known(f) :- ar_type(f, "varchar"), !ar_len_unknown(f).
ar_known(f) :- ar_dec(f, _, _, _, _).

// ar_rewrite(o, n): changing a column from field call o to field call n rewrites the table.
.decl ar_rewrite(o: node, n: node)
ar_rewrite(fo, fn) :- ar_pair(fo, fn), ar_type(fo, a), ar_type(fn, b), a != b, !ar_coercible(a, b),
    !ar_same_target(fo, fn).
// ar_same_target(fo, fn): both calls are relations to one model: the column follows that key either way.
.decl ar_same_target(fo: node, fn: node)
ar_same_target(fo, fn) :- ar_pair(fo, fn), dj_fk_target(fo, m), dj_fk_target(fn, m).
ar_rewrite(fo, fn) :- ar_pair(fo, fn), ar_type(fo, "text"), ar_len(fn, _, _).
ar_rewrite(fo, fn) :- ar_pair(fo, fn), ar_len(fo, a, _), ar_len(fn, b, _), b < a.
ar_rewrite(fo, fn) :- ar_pair(fo, fn), ar_unlimited(fo), ar_len(fn, _, _).
ar_rewrite(fo, fn) :- ar_pair(fo, fn), ar_dec(fo, p, s, _, _), ar_dec(fn, p2, s2, _, _), (s2 != s ; p2 < p).
// ar_pair(o, n): a judged change: an AlterField's call n and its nearest earlier definition's call o, both known.
.decl ar_pair(o: node, n: node)
ar_pair(fo, fn) :- dj_field_old(o, fo), ar_alter(o, _, _, _, _, fn), ar_known(fo), ar_known(fn).
// ar_coercible(a, b): PostgreSQL changes type a to b in the catalog (varchar to text; text to an unlimited varchar,
// which a limited one rewrites above).
.decl ar_coercible(a: symbol, b: symbol)
ar_coercible("varchar", "text"). ar_coercible("text", "varchar").

// ar_label(f, l): how the message names field call f: its class, with its length or precision when they matter.
.decl ar_label(f: node, l: symbol)
ar_label(f, l) :- ar_cls(f, t), !dj_fk_class(t), ar_type(f, y), y != "varchar", y != "numeric", l = t.
ar_label(f, l) :- ar_cls(f, t), dj_fk_class(t), ar_fk_type(f, y), l = cat(cat(cat(t, " ("), y), ")").
ar_label(f, l) :- ar_cls(f, t), call_arg(f, -1, "max_length", _), ar_len(f, _, s),
    l = cat(cat(cat(t, "(max_length="), s), ")").
ar_label(f, l) :- ar_cls(f, t), !call_arg(f, -1, "max_length", _), ar_len(f, _, s),
    l = cat(cat(cat(t, " ("), s), " characters)").
ar_label(f, l) :- ar_cls(f, t), ar_unlimited(f), l = cat(t, " (unlimited)").
ar_label(f, l) :- ar_cls(f, t), ar_dec(f, _, _, tp, ts),
    l = cat(cat(cat(cat(cat(t, "(max_digits="), tp), ", decimal_places="), ts), ")").

// The cases, `cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/`, read as one repository: each line ending in
// `# caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "billing/__init__.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/billing/__init__.py"
    .fixture "shop/__init__.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/__init__.py"
    .fixture "shop/tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "shop/config.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/config.py"
    .fixture "shop/fields.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/fields.py"
    .fixture "billing/migrations/0001_initial.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/billing/migrations/0001_initial.py"
    .fixture "billing/migrations/0002_order_amount.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/billing/migrations/0002_order_amount.py"
    .fixture "billing/migrations/0002_squashed_0004.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/billing/migrations/0002_squashed_0004.py"
    .fixture "billing/migrations/0005_after_squash.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/billing/migrations/0005_after_squash.py"
    .fixture "billing/migrations/__init__.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/billing/migrations/__init__.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0001_initial.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0001_initial.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0002_order_legacy_id.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0002_order_legacy_id.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0004_state_only.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0004_state_only.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0005_rename_nickname.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0005_rename_nickname.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0006_widen.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0006_widen.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0007_siteconfig.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0007_siteconfig.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0008_siteconfig_bigint.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0008_siteconfig_bigint.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0009_order_refs.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0009_order_refs.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0010_custom_fields.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0010_custom_fields.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0011_rename_blurb.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/0011_rename_blurb.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/__init__.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/migrations/__init__.py"
    .fixture "shop/tests/migrations/0001_initial.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/tests/migrations/0001_initial.py"
    .fixture "shop/tests/migrations/0002_widget_bigint.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/tests/migrations/0002_widget_bigint.py"
    .fixture "shop/tests/migrations/__init__.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/shop/tests/migrations/__init__.py"
    .expect _ at "billing/migrations/0002_order_amount.py":17
    .expect _ at "billing/migrations/0005_after_squash.py":12
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":12
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":17
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":22
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":24
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":28
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":33
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":38
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":44
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":49
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":54
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":59
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":64
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":69
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":74
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":79
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0003_alter_types.py":84
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0004_state_only.py":21
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0006_widen.py":23
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0008_siteconfig_bigint.py":18
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0009_order_refs.py":14
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0010_custom_fields.py":21
    .expect _ at "shop/migrations/0011_rename_blurb.py":13
.end

// A project that configures MySQL only: the same int → bigint change stays silent.
.test mysql_only exactly
    .fixture "settings.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/mysql_only/settings.py"
    .fixture "shop/__init__.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/mysql_only/shop/__init__.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/__init__.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/mysql_only/shop/migrations/__init__.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0001_initial.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/mysql_only/shop/migrations/0001_initial.py"
    .fixture "shop/migrations/0002_rating_score_bigint.py" from "../cases/django-practice-alterfield-rewrites-table/mysql_only/shop/migrations/0002_rating_score_bigint.py"
.end
